+class EntityHop1Query(dspy.Signature):
+    """You are retrieving Wikipedia documents to verify a multi-hop claim.
+
+    Hop 1 retrieved Wikipedia passages for the raw claim. Many multi-hop claims
+    pivot on a single MAIN entity whose bare name is ambiguous and was not
+    disambiguated by the raw-claim retrieval. Emit ONE disambiguation search
+    query for the claim's MAIN entity, choosing the single best Wikipedia
+    archetype from this fixed family:
+    - "<entity> (musical)"          (a stage musical)
+    - "<entity> (TV series)"        (a television series)
+    - "<entity> (song)"
+    - "<entity> (film)"
+    - "<entity> (band)"              (a musical group / band)
+    - "<entity> (video game)"
+    - "<entity> (board game)"
+    - "<entity> (novel)"
+    - "<entity> <year/season> season"  (a sports season article)
+    - "<entity> (county)" / "<entity> (place)"  (a county or geographic place)
+    - "<entity>"                     (bare person — a biography article)
+
+    Use the claim and the list of `retrieved_titles` already fetched by hop 1 so
+    the query does NOT duplicate hop 1's siblings. The main entity is the subject
+    the claim is fundamentally about. Pick the archetype that best matches the
+    claim's domain. Keep the entity name verbatim; only vary the archetype suffix.
+
+    Escape clause: output "none" for the query when the main entity is clearly
+    unambiguous (its bare name already resolves to the right Wikipedia article,
+    or no archetype fits the claim).
+
+    Output a single concise disambiguation query (the entity name plus the
+    chosen archetype), or "none"."""
+    claim: str = dspy.InputField()
+    retrieved_titles: list[str] = dspy.InputField(desc="Wikipedia article titles already retrieved in hop 1")
+    query: str = dspy.OutputField(desc="A single disambiguation query for the claim's main entity, or 'none'")
+
