+    2. Sports-season article: e.g. "2001-02 Detroit Red Wings season".
+    3. A song or other work adapted from a retrieved work (e.g. its parent work,
+       or a cover/adaptation).
+    4. A predecessor, parent, or subsidiary organization of a retrieved
+       organization.
+    5. A co-starring film: a film that two retrieved people both starred in.
+    6. A city or county implied by a place reference in the claim or passages.
+
+    Two hints (NOT from the training subsample, illustrative only):
+    - claim implies a 1986 NASA launch failure -> "Space Shuttle Challenger disaster"
+    - claim implies a 2001-02 NHL team season   -> "2001-02 Detroit Red Wings season"
+    - claim implies a Tom Hanks 1998 war film   -> "Saving Private Ryan"
+
+    Use the claim, the truncated `titles` list (retrieved titles), and the
+    truncated `passages_text`. The implied entity's article must NOT be among the
+    retrieved titles. Output a single short search query phrase, or "none" if no
+    implied entity is plausibly part of the chain.
+
+    Output ONE short search query phrase (not the whole claim), or "none"."""
